WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
(dramatic music)
(whooshing sounds)

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.440
- [Narrator] After months of delays,

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.720
SpaceX received word from regulators

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.270
about the fate of its
Starbase launch site.

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.763
- It's a pretty big deal for the company.

00:00:10.763 --> 00:00:14.550
And the FAA basically gave
the company the green light

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:15.720
to move forward.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.760
- [Narrator] On Monday, the FAA released

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.980
its final environmental assessment

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.350
of the company's south Texas location.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.570
The assessment found
that continued launches

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:28.620
at the Boca Chica would not
significantly affect the quality

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.240
of the human environment.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.170
- It was a big hurdle.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.110
I mean, it created a fair amount

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.470
of I guess you'd call little
a regulatory uncertainty.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:41.370
It means that SpaceX has a pathway forward

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.500
to start the kind of testing

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.790
to show that this gigantic
rocket really can work.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.110
- [Narrator] The agency's assessment

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:52.500
also found that before it
can start orbital launches,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.770
SpaceX must carry out more than 75 actions

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:56.880
to mitigate the effects

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.270
of the launches on the
surrounding area and environment.

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.730
These actions read from noise restrictions

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.430
to monitoring the lighting
at the launch site

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.310
to preparing a report on
historic events that took place

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.070
in the area during the
Mexican-American War

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.930
and the Civil War.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:16.140
So what does this
assessment mean for SpaceX

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.780
and the Starship program going forward?

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.330
Moreover, what does it
mean for NASA's plan

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:25.195
to get the US back to the moon by 2025?

00:01:25.195 --> 00:01:26.850
(dramatic music)

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:30.180
Last year, SpaceX CEO Elon Musk announced

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.850
that he was creating a
new city called Starbase

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.230
at Boca Chica Village

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.470
in an unincorporated
community of about 30 homes

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.590
located next to the
southernmost beach in Texas.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.420
- [Announcer] Lift off of the Falcon 9.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.280
- [Narrator] SpaceX originally planned

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.870
to use the site for launches

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.750
of its Falcon 9 and Falcon Heavy rockets

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.120
but later, it decided to use Starbase

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.453
to develop its much larger
Starship spacecraft.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:59.910
SpaceX has been conducting
suborbital Starship launches

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.850
at Boca Chica since 2019.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.370
But for the spaceship's
development to continue,

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.130
the FAA requires additional permitting.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.657
- Starship is the biggest

00:02:10.657 --> 00:02:15.330
and most powerful rocket system
SpaceX has ever developed.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.890
It's meant for some

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:20.944
of the company's most
ambitious deep space missions.

00:02:20.944 --> 00:02:22.770
(dramatic music)

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.570
- [Narrator] Although
many in the state welcomed

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.910
the increase investment and jobs,

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.040
some in south Texas are concerned

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.950
that SpaceX's expansion
will come at a steep price

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.000
to the environment.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.590
- One of the major concerns

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:38.070
is that the FAA hasn't
done enough analysis

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:39.310
of what the effects

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.910
of operating Starship from
this location would be.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.440
- [Narrator] Boca Chica sits at the edge

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.600
of a national wildlife refuge

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.680
but since SpaceX began expanding
its operations in 2019,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.240
some conservationists worry

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.280
that the eventual environmental impact

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.013
will be devastating.

00:02:58.013 --> 00:02:59.130
(booming sound)

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.440
The FAA's final environmental assessment

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.880
of the Boca Chica site

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.500
was expected last year.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.710
However, the agency pushed
back the deadline five times,

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.860
saying SpaceX made
changes to its application

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.080
that required additional analysis.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:13.913
- One of the big reasons

00:03:13.913 --> 00:03:16.080
that this has been delayed multiple times

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.830
is because the FAA has
said almost 20,000 people

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.570
have weighed in on this,

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:24.570
and provided public comment for, against,

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.120
and they had to go through those.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.830
- [Narrator] The breadth
of submissions range

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:31.440
from opposition by a wildlife biologist

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.600
to support from an engineer.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.910
Others were submitted on behalf of groups

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.610
and many were pages long.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.500
The completion of the assessment

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.600
does not guarantee that the FAA

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.030
will issue SpaceX a launch license.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.720
SpaceX's application must
also meet FAA safety,

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.240
risk and financial requirements.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.700
SpaceX expects the first orbital launch

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.110
of its Starship spacecraft

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.180
to take place later this year.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:00.300
Starship is designed for
voyages to the moon and Mars

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.580
and NASA selected Starship

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:05.640
to return humans to the moon in 2025.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.950
- They can't start launching immediately.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.080
It's not quite that simple.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.250
The company also has to
make sure it's compliant

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.070
with all of these actions.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.840
So they still have some steps

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.660
to go before they start launching.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.220
- [Narrator] SpaceX did not respond

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.140
to multiple requests for comment

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.450
but shortly after the FAA's decision,

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.820
the company did tweet that Starship

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:33.518
was one step closer to
its first orbital flight.

00:04:33.518 --> 00:04:36.268
(dramatic music)

00:04:38.353 --> 00:04:40.991
(whooshing sound)

